---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Copyright | Kvisl" description="Copyright, quotation, licensing, and reuse rules for Kvisl.">
  <main class="container page-main narrow-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Policy</p>
    <h1 class="page-title">Copyright</h1>
    <p class="policy-updated">Last updated 19 September 2026</p>

    <div class="policy-copy">
      <p>Unless a page states otherwise, original <span class="notranslate" translate="no">Kvisl</span> writing, editing, curation, design, graphics, branding, and other original publication material are protected by copyright and related rights.</p>

      <div class="policy-contact-box">
        <strong>Rights and licensing</strong>
        <a href="mailto:hello@kvisl.com">hello@kvisl.com</a>
      </div>

      <h2>1. Ownership</h2>
      <p>Rights may belong to <span class="notranslate" translate="no">Kvisl</span>, an individual author, illustrator, photographer, contributor, licensor, or another rights holder. Credits on an article or image may identify the relevant owner or source.</p>

      <h2>2. Reasonable quotation</h2>
      <p>Reasonable quotation is permitted where allowed by law when the excerpt is proportionate to the purpose, preserves context, and clearly credits the author, article title, and <span class="notranslate" translate="no">Kvisl</span>. Online quotations should link to the canonical article where practical.</p>

      <h2>3. Republication</h2>
      <p>Full republication or substantial reproduction requires prior written permission unless a legal exception clearly applies. Licensing starts at US$600 per article and may be higher depending on the work, <span class="notranslate" translate="no">Kvisl</span>'s editorial and creative contribution, the original author's terms, territory, language, medium, audience, duration, exclusivity, and intended use.</p>
      <p>Payment alone does not create a licence. Permission takes effect only after <span class="notranslate" translate="no">Kvisl</span> confirms the authorised use in writing and any required payment has been completed.</p>

      <h2>4. Translation, adaptation, and derivative use</h2>
      <p>Translations, abridgements, adaptations, audio or video versions, anthology use, commercial educational use, syndication, and other derivative uses require separate approval. We may require author review, and every approved version must preserve the agreed attribution.</p>

      <h2>5. Images and third-party material</h2>
      <p>Photographs, illustrations, embedded media, quotations, datasets, and other third-party material may be subject to separate rights. A licence to republish article text does not automatically include those materials unless the written agreement expressly says so.</p>

      <h2>6. Branding</h2>
      <p>The <span class="notranslate" translate="no">Kvisl</span> name, logo, visual identity, and trade dress may not be used in a way that implies sponsorship, endorsement, partnership, or official status without written permission.</p>

      <h2>7. Copyright and rights complaints</h2>
      <p>If you believe material on the site infringes your rights, email <a href="mailto:hello@kvisl.com">hello@kvisl.com</a> and include:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>your name and reliable contact information;</li>
        <li>identification of the work or right you claim;</li>
        <li>the exact <span class="notranslate" translate="no">Kvisl</span> URL or material you are reporting;</li>
        <li>an explanation of why you believe the use is unauthorised;</li>
        <li>any ownership, agency, or licensing information that helps us assess the claim.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We may ask for additional information before acting. Knowingly false or misleading notices may have legal consequences.</p>

      <h2>8. Permissions</h2>
      <p>For quotation beyond ordinary fair-use or fair-dealing limits, republication, translation, classroom reproduction, commercial use, or other rights enquiries, email <a href="mailto:hello@kvisl.com">hello@kvisl.com</a> or use the <a href="/republish">Republish</a> form.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
